-- title:
--   Étale j-level sets on the mod ℓ j-chart of X₀(p)
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ and $\ell$ be primes with $\ell \neq p$. Write $F =$ `modularFunctionFieldFull p` for the intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q} \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\mathbb{Q}$ generated by the Laurent expansions $\mathrm{qExpand}\,\mathbb{Q}\,d\,j_q$ for the divisors $d$ of $p$, let $j_{\mathrm{Full}}(p) \in F$ be the element given by the $q$-expansion $j_q$ of the modular invariant, and let $A_{\mathrm{fin}}(p)$ be the finite-chart $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra $\mathrm{chartAlg}\,\mathbb{Z}\,F\,\{j_{\mathrm{Full}}(p)\}$ of $F$, the coordinate ring of the finite chart in the two-chart integral model, with $j_{\mathrm{Full}}(p)$ regarded as the element `jChartFin` of it. The assertion is that there exists a nonzero polynomial $a \in (\mathbb{Z}/\ell)[X]$ such that for every monic $g \in \mathbb{Z}[X]$ whose reduction $\bar g \in (\mathbb{Z}/\ell)[X]$ is separable and coprime to $a$, the $\mathbb{Z}/\ell$-algebra $$\bigl((\mathbb{Z}/\ell) \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}} A_{\mathrm{fin}}(p)\bigr) \big/ \bigl(1 \otimes g(j_{\mathrm{Full}}(p))\bigr),$$ the quotient by the ideal generated by the single element $1 \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}} \mathrm{aeval}\,(\mathrm{jChartFin})\,g$, is étale over $\mathbb{Z}/\ell$. The polynomial $a$ is chosen once and for all, before $g$; no further hypothesis is put on $g$ beyond monicity and the two conditions on $\bar g$.
--
--   This is Igusa's good reduction of $X_0(p)$ at a prime $\ell \nmid p$, expressed in the currency of the finite-$j$ chart ring: away from a fixed finite set of values of $j$ (the zero locus of the avoidance polynomial $a$) and away from multiple roots of $\bar g$, the level set $\{g(j) = 0\}$ in the mod $\ell$ fibre is an étale $\mathbb{F}_\ell$-scheme. It feeds the construction of finite étale level rings, [`ModularCurve.HpoolLevelRing.exists_finite_etale_levelRing_jChartFin`](thm.html#ModularCurve.HpoolLevelRing.exists_finite_etale_levelRing_jChartFin).
